From 7cc4bafde8942e5c880a8a9f4c5231f5e0516f57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qualcomm-toolbox <169756160+qcom-toolbox@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:10:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] umi-0175-adreno-nativeabi-turnip-metal

The NativeAdreno ABI v1 (SweetGPUABI.h, UniXNU drivers/NativeAdreno, MIT,
as ios-flame serves it) on top of the SweetAdreno C API, so Turnip's darwin
backend (Mesa tu_knl_darwin.cc) can talk to this kernel, plus the Metal
plugin properties that make MTLRegisterDevices load metal2vulkan's
SweetMetal2 bundle (boot-arg sweetmtl, default off; without it Metal passes
the accelerator over as before).

sweet_adreno.c grows the v2 needs: per-client 4 GB GPU windows from 8 GB
(sweet_adreno_window_alloc), arbitrary pages mapped at client-chosen
addresses 4K at a time (map_at/unmap_at), multi-IB submits with one
CACHE_FLUSH_TS fence and ring-room handling (submit_v2), nanosecond fence
waits, the CP always-on counter as the timestamp (0x0980/0x0981) and a
fault counter for GetStatus. SweetAdreno.cpp opens v2 clients with type
0x4147 ('AG') or 2 and serves Query/GetDeviceInfo/BoAlloc/BoImport/BoMap/
BoFree/BoCpuMap/BoCpuUnmap/Submit (16 IBs, overlapping BOs cleaned before
the GPU reads them)/WaitFence/GetTimestamp/GetStatus/Metadata/queues.
A650 values: chip 0x06050002, gmem 0x120000, uche trap base as step 20
programs it, hbb 16, UBWC 4 swizzle 6; gmem_base 0x100000 follows flame's
A640 and is to be verified against Mesa's fd_dev_info when Turnip builds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
